1
00:00:00,063 --> 00:00:01,054
(All characters, locations,
and events are fictional

2
00:00:01,079 --> 00:00:02,031
and for entertainment
purposes only.

3
00:00:02,055 --> 00:00:03,070
No actions depicted are intended
to be encouraged or endorsed.

4
00:00:03,095 --> 00:00:04,189
Animals were specially trained
and supervised by professionals.

5
00:00:04,214 --> 00:00:05,570
Viewer discretion is advised.)

6
00:00:07,034 --> 00:00:09,531
A lot of people say golf
is all about competition.

7
00:00:10,523 --> 00:00:13,167
But to me,
it's really a test of heart.

8
00:00:14,882 --> 00:00:17,856
Some holes feel too long.
Sometimes the wind is too strong.

9
00:00:19,627 --> 00:00:22,893
But if you never swing, you've
already lost before you begin.

10
00:00:24,273 --> 00:00:26,157
Love is probably no different.

11
00:00:26,659 --> 00:00:28,662
Even if you don't know
whether it'll find the hole,

12
00:00:28,687 --> 00:00:31,092
you still have to be brave enough
to take the first shot.

13
00:00:32,442 --> 00:00:34,087
Whatever the outcome,

14
00:00:34,111 --> 00:00:36,111
all you can do is accept it.

15
00:00:42,229 --> 00:00:44,476
(Pro Sherry: Tiranan Yoopan)

16
00:00:54,885 --> 00:00:58,297
♪ Everyone can tell
by the way you stare ♪

17
00:00:59,022 --> 00:01:00,746
♪ Sneaking little looks
when I'm unaware ♪

18
00:01:00,771 --> 00:01:04,225
♪ It's plain to see ♪

19
00:01:04,886 --> 00:01:06,545
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

20
00:01:06,570 --> 00:01:09,970
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

21
00:01:10,654 --> 00:01:12,369
♪ You remember
every fave of mine ♪

22
00:01:12,394 --> 00:01:15,934
♪ Everywhere I go,
you're by my side ♪

23
00:01:16,351 --> 00:01:18,153
♪ Don't tell me
there's nothing on your mind ♪

24
00:01:18,178 --> 00:01:21,107
♪ So when are you
gonna say the words? ♪

25
00:01:21,132 --> 00:01:22,991
♪ Don't keep me waiting
till it hurts ♪

26
00:01:23,016 --> 00:01:25,804
♪ The way you act,
I know you're into me ♪

27
00:01:25,829 --> 00:01:28,712
♪ That racing heart
gives you away so easily ♪

28
00:01:28,737 --> 00:01:32,555
♪ But I'll play clueless,
just wait and see ♪

29
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:34,580
♪ I wanna hear you say it to me ♪

30
00:01:34,605 --> 00:01:37,426
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

31
00:01:37,451 --> 00:01:40,930
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

32
00:01:40,955 --> 00:01:45,640
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

33
00:01:45,665 --> 00:01:47,665
♪ Or should I be the one
to call your bluff? ♪

34
00:01:49,072 --> 00:01:51,996
Stay calm. Focus on
the shot in front of you.

35
00:01:54,593 --> 00:01:56,772
Six strokes on a par five.

36
00:01:56,797 --> 00:01:59,386
Two better than the limit
I gave you. You did it.

37
00:01:59,411 --> 00:02:02,515
Yes! I did it! I actually did it!

38
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:05,733
See? When you really commit,
nothing is impossible.

39
00:02:05,758 --> 00:02:09,865
Your swing is steadier, and your
timing is much better. Good job.

40
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:11,760
Who have you been learning from?

41
00:02:11,785 --> 00:02:13,783
Pro Jin at The Royal Green.

42
00:02:13,808 --> 00:02:16,689
You can't invite her here.
Those two don't get along.

43
00:02:16,968 --> 00:02:18,262
Who doesn't?

44
00:02:18,287 --> 00:02:21,151
Pro Vee and Pro Jin.

45
00:02:21,176 --> 00:02:24,150
I heard Nana
took a lesson from you.

46
00:02:24,175 --> 00:02:27,256
You're good. You figured out
your student pretty quickly.

47
00:02:27,281 --> 00:02:28,803
Too bad I couldn't read
my own friend

48
00:02:28,828 --> 00:02:31,339
before she betrayed me, even
after knowing her for so long.

49
00:02:31,364 --> 00:02:32,632
Miss Nana, we've got a problem.

50
00:02:32,657 --> 00:02:34,213
The tour group
that booked our course

51
00:02:34,238 --> 00:02:35,746
just canceled
the entire reservation.

52
00:02:39,863 --> 00:02:44,931
Everyone, we're not here today
for me to tell you what to do.

53
00:02:45,111 --> 00:02:46,680
We're here
to figure it out together.

54
00:02:46,705 --> 00:02:50,030
How do we make Goodview number
one again, like it used to be?

55
00:02:50,055 --> 00:02:51,719
We're not doing this
just for the course.

56
00:02:51,744 --> 00:02:53,154
We're doing it for ourselves.

57
00:02:53,178 --> 00:02:55,113
Because if the course
becomes profitable again,

58
00:02:55,138 --> 00:02:58,357
all of us benefit from
the rewards that come with it.

59
00:02:58,590 --> 00:03:03,371
Our goal is to make this a place
everyone wants to come to,

60
00:03:03,396 --> 00:03:05,303
golfers and non-golfers alike.

61
00:03:05,328 --> 00:03:08,983
So no idea is too wild
or too unconventional.

62
00:03:09,008 --> 00:03:10,403
Our first response
will always be,

63
00:03:10,428 --> 00:03:11,744
"That's a good idea."

64
00:03:12,188 --> 00:03:13,984
Then we'll build on it together.

65
00:03:14,009 --> 00:03:15,920
No shooting ideas down.
No arguing against them.

66
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:18,518
Each group gets one hour.

67
00:03:18,543 --> 00:03:19,637
Go ahead.

68
00:03:41,761 --> 00:03:43,664
Every idea we hear...

69
00:03:43,689 --> 00:03:46,244
- is a good idea.
- is a good idea.

70
00:03:46,571 --> 00:03:48,439
Our group's idea is
"Date on the Green."

71
00:03:48,638 --> 00:03:50,090
This one's from my team.

72
00:03:50,115 --> 00:03:51,604
That's a good idea.

73
00:03:51,629 --> 00:03:54,302
We'd offer date packages
for couples at the course.

74
00:03:54,327 --> 00:03:57,183
A lot of couples are looking
for new places to go on dates.

75
00:03:57,208 --> 00:03:59,920
We already have meal sets
and photographers ready to go.

76
00:03:59,945 --> 00:04:01,404
I like it. Sold.

77
00:04:02,502 --> 00:04:04,232
And by late afternoon or evening,

78
00:04:04,257 --> 00:04:06,115
most golfers are already
done for the day.

79
00:04:06,139 --> 00:04:08,004
It's better than leaving
the course empty.

80
00:04:08,029 --> 00:04:09,556
I think it's a great idea.

81
00:04:09,698 --> 00:04:12,035
Thank you.

82
00:04:12,942 --> 00:04:14,465
As for this team...

83
00:04:15,095 --> 00:04:17,063
"Caddie in Character."

84
00:04:17,088 --> 00:04:20,825
We'd divide our caddies
into four different styles

85
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:22,832
for different types of golfers.

86
00:04:22,857 --> 00:04:25,064
- Exactly.
- Nice.

87
00:04:25,247 --> 00:04:27,104
Based on customer feedback,

88
00:04:27,129 --> 00:04:29,207
people want caddies
who can read the room.

89
00:04:29,274 --> 00:04:31,854
Some days,
golfers want a quiet round,

90
00:04:31,879 --> 00:04:33,538
but the caddie keeps chatting.

91
00:04:33,569 --> 00:04:36,479
Sometimes they want advice
on a particular shot,

92
00:04:36,504 --> 00:04:38,645
but the caddie doesn't know
the course well enough.

93
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:41,421
And sometimes the caddie
should help set the mood,

94
00:04:41,446 --> 00:04:43,184
because some major business deals

95
00:04:43,209 --> 00:04:44,712
get closed right here
on the course.

96
00:04:44,736 --> 00:04:48,960
Hmm...
And if the clients are happy,

97
00:04:48,985 --> 00:04:51,209
the caddies might even
get bigger tips.

98
00:04:52,298 --> 00:04:53,314
Good.

99
00:04:54,273 --> 00:04:56,499
As for Pro Jin's Golf Academy,

100
00:04:57,134 --> 00:04:58,586
that's a no-brainer.

101
00:04:59,250 --> 00:05:01,673
We'll also have tailored programs

102
00:05:01,698 --> 00:05:05,786
for kids, teens, women,
and business professionals.

103
00:05:05,811 --> 00:05:07,463
Let's move forward with it.

104
00:05:07,709 --> 00:05:10,070
I'd like to add
a program for seniors too.

105
00:05:10,570 --> 00:05:13,244
They're another group
we should be focusing on.

106
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:15,504
Good. That's a good idea.

107
00:05:16,856 --> 00:05:20,422
And from my darling August's
team, we have Golf E-Sports.

108
00:05:21,207 --> 00:05:23,919
We'll recreate our course
in an online golf game.

109
00:05:24,126 --> 00:05:27,799
Then I've got E-Food.
That's my idea.

110
00:05:27,824 --> 00:05:31,242
We photograph our dishes
and put the menu online.

111
00:05:31,267 --> 00:05:34,729
People coming to the course
can order their food in advance.

112
00:05:34,754 --> 00:05:39,147
And even if they're not coming,
they can still order delivery.

113
00:05:39,273 --> 00:05:41,167
- Can our team handle that?
- Absolutely.

114
00:05:41,192 --> 00:05:43,937
- There you go.
- Good. That's a great idea.

115
00:05:46,058 --> 00:05:48,912
As for Pro Vee's group,
I'm not quite following yet.

116
00:05:48,937 --> 00:05:51,216
Could you explain it
a little more?

117
00:05:51,389 --> 00:05:54,898
It's not really a new idea.
A lot of courses already do it.

118
00:05:54,923 --> 00:05:56,907
We used to do it here too.

119
00:05:56,946 --> 00:06:00,356
But I think bringing it back
could add some excitement.

120
00:06:00,381 --> 00:06:02,745
Great. That's a good idea.
Approved.

121
00:06:02,770 --> 00:06:04,376
She hasn't even told you
the idea yet.

122
00:06:04,401 --> 00:06:07,163
Oh. Right. Go ahead.

123
00:06:07,311 --> 00:06:08,404
A Pro-Am.

124
00:06:09,254 --> 00:06:11,716
Pro Am?
We have a pro named Am here?

125
00:06:11,741 --> 00:06:13,773
I thought we only had Pro Vee,
Pro Jin, and Pro...

126
00:06:13,798 --> 00:06:17,991
No, no. A Pro-Am is an event
where amateur golfers

127
00:06:18,016 --> 00:06:20,637
get paired up
with professional golfers.

128
00:06:20,662 --> 00:06:24,109
They could be pros from our
course or guest pros we invite.

129
00:06:24,547 --> 00:06:26,110
Normally, at these events,

130
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:31,097
they invite sponsors,
major partners, and the media.

131
00:06:31,122 --> 00:06:35,539
But ours would also give
regular golfers at our course

132
00:06:35,564 --> 00:06:37,333
the chance to play a round
with a pro.

133
00:06:37,829 --> 00:06:40,108
We could charge an additional fee

134
00:06:40,133 --> 00:06:42,910
and hold it on special occasions.

135
00:06:46,338 --> 00:06:49,426
But won't all the pretty pros
get hit on?

136
00:06:50,888 --> 00:06:53,217
Hmm? Jealous?

137
00:06:53,955 --> 00:06:56,331
- Concerned.
- Sure.

138
00:07:03,804 --> 00:07:05,882
I've got an idea too.

139
00:07:06,350 --> 00:07:08,755
I'd like to propose
a Night Golf project.

140
00:07:09,149 --> 00:07:11,388
But it won't just be playing
under the lights at night.

141
00:07:11,413 --> 00:07:14,977
We'll also have handsome male
caddies looking after our guests.

142
00:07:20,506 --> 00:07:23,885
Before anyone gets
the wrong idea, let me explain.

143
00:07:24,528 --> 00:07:28,166
I don't want us to assume
that having men serve women

144
00:07:28,191 --> 00:07:30,064
or women serve men

145
00:07:30,089 --> 00:07:32,656
always has to be sexual.

146
00:07:32,681 --> 00:07:35,849
Sometimes it's simply
another form of entertainment

147
00:07:35,874 --> 00:07:38,440
that makes people feel confident
and brings positive energy.

148
00:07:38,465 --> 00:07:40,879
We're not selling sex.
We're not selling looks.

149
00:07:40,904 --> 00:07:44,787
We're selling atmosphere, fun,
and the feeling of being special.

150
00:07:45,097 --> 00:07:49,710
Golf courses have traditionally
been seen as a man's space.

151
00:07:49,735 --> 00:07:53,263
I want women to feel that
this place belongs to them too.

152
00:07:53,288 --> 00:07:55,402
Not by diminishing men,

153
00:07:55,427 --> 00:07:57,214
but by bringing in
something fresh.

154
00:07:57,239 --> 00:07:58,795
If I may add something,

155
00:07:58,820 --> 00:08:01,013
the female golf market
is growing every year.

156
00:08:01,038 --> 00:08:03,276
Nightlife experiences
are also becoming more popular,

157
00:08:03,301 --> 00:08:05,396
and younger customers are looking
for activities

158
00:08:05,421 --> 00:08:07,503
worth photographing and sharing.

159
00:08:07,527 --> 00:08:09,229
I think it's a great idea.

160
00:08:09,254 --> 00:08:12,184
We can position golf as
entertainment, as something fun,

161
00:08:12,209 --> 00:08:14,637
and create a new image for golf.

162
00:08:14,662 --> 00:08:16,821
Instead of going out
to a pub or bar,

163
00:08:16,846 --> 00:08:18,727
why not come to a golf course?

164
00:08:18,752 --> 00:08:20,825
I'll summarize all of
today's ideas

165
00:08:20,850 --> 00:08:24,512
and put together a proposal
for the management team.

166
00:08:24,774 --> 00:08:26,774
Including the budget
and timeline.

167
00:08:26,970 --> 00:08:28,168
Thanks, Belle.

168
00:08:29,996 --> 00:08:32,869
And thank you, everyone,
for sharing your ideas today.

169
00:08:33,067 --> 00:08:36,430
Goodview is going to be one
of the top golf courses again.

170
00:08:37,042 --> 00:08:38,360
Allez, allez!

171
00:08:38,385 --> 00:08:41,289
- Huh?
- What does that mean?

172
00:08:42,011 --> 00:08:45,575
"Allez, allez" is French for
"Come on, everyone! Let's go!"

173
00:08:45,734 --> 00:08:49,244
All right, everyone. We've got
a new one. One, two, three...

174
00:08:49,420 --> 00:08:52,120
Allez, allez!

175
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:46,729
The breaker looks fine.

176
00:09:47,332 --> 00:09:50,062
Why is your power out?
Mine's still on.

177
00:09:50,558 --> 00:09:52,068
Do you know how to fix it?

178
00:09:55,061 --> 00:09:56,594
I'm not an electrician.

179
00:09:57,498 --> 00:09:59,424
Shouldn't you call one?

180
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,035
It's really late.

181
00:10:02,430 --> 00:10:04,399
I'd feel bad
calling them out now.

182
00:10:04,424 --> 00:10:05,819
But you don't feel bad
calling me?

183
00:10:08,491 --> 00:10:10,079
Wait, wait.

184
00:10:11,774 --> 00:10:15,567
You said the power at your place
is still on, right?

185
00:10:22,177 --> 00:10:24,934
Then can I stay over tonight?

186
00:10:29,378 --> 00:10:30,783
Make yourself at home, Pro Vee.

187
00:10:31,045 --> 00:10:33,045
Shouldn't I
be the one saying that?

188
00:10:52,803 --> 00:10:54,062
I'm turning the light off.

189
00:10:57,762 --> 00:10:59,432
Chomp, chomp.

190
00:11:02,218 --> 00:11:03,396
What are you doing?

191
00:11:03,658 --> 00:11:05,606
You never played this
when you were little?

192
00:11:05,836 --> 00:11:07,836
Chomp, chomp.

193
00:11:08,298 --> 00:11:09,872
You're such a kid.

194
00:11:10,089 --> 00:11:12,374
Oh, so you've never done it.

195
00:11:13,242 --> 00:11:16,075
Or maybe...
you just don't know how.

196
00:11:21,003 --> 00:11:23,751
Wow. Did you really
have to show off?

197
00:11:24,748 --> 00:11:27,017
Fine. Then try this.

198
00:11:29,103 --> 00:11:30,696
How about...

199
00:11:32,111 --> 00:11:34,111
Let her hold on to you.

200
00:11:47,774 --> 00:11:51,365
Ow! Don't pinch her. That hurts!

201
00:11:55,943 --> 00:11:57,714
Can you do this one, Pro Vee?

202
00:12:21,363 --> 00:12:22,377
Let's just sleep.

203
00:12:23,848 --> 00:12:24,895
Oh.

204
00:12:58,634 --> 00:13:00,648
I put this here in case
you felt uncomfortable.

205
00:13:01,132 --> 00:13:03,131
Do I look that uncomfortable?

206
00:13:03,782 --> 00:13:08,932
Not really.
Just a little awkward.

207
00:13:09,904 --> 00:13:10,930
Pro Vee...

208
00:13:12,057 --> 00:13:15,676
I'm kidding.
You did really well today.

209
00:13:16,680 --> 00:13:20,396
- With what?
- The brainstorming workshop.

210
00:13:20,421 --> 00:13:23,035
I haven't seen everyone
that energized in a long time.

211
00:13:23,187 --> 00:13:25,864
And I'm going to make
all their ideas happen.

212
00:13:25,889 --> 00:13:27,398
Just watch me.

213
00:13:28,134 --> 00:13:31,401
I will. Now go to sleep.

214
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:34,549
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

215
00:14:34,574 --> 00:14:37,322
Ooh, new look, new uniforms.
So bright and fresh!

216
00:14:37,347 --> 00:14:39,306
- Yes.
- Oh, and what's this?

217
00:14:39,331 --> 00:14:41,513
This is our new
air-conditioned golf cart.

218
00:14:41,538 --> 00:14:43,985
We're the first course
in Thailand to use this model.

219
00:14:44,010 --> 00:14:45,431
Wow. Very nice.

220
00:14:45,456 --> 00:14:47,298
Which caddie mode
would you like today?

221
00:14:47,323 --> 00:14:48,337
Serious mode.

222
00:14:48,362 --> 00:14:50,209
I've got a tournament
at the end of the month.

223
00:14:50,234 --> 00:14:52,967
- You got it. Hop in.
- Let's go.

224
00:14:57,626 --> 00:15:00,084
- Let me turn the AC on for you.
- Please do.

225
00:15:04,392 --> 00:15:07,769
- Cool enough?
- Wow, that's strong. And cold!

226
00:15:07,808 --> 00:15:09,779
No waiting for it
to cool down either. Very nice.

227
00:15:09,811 --> 00:15:11,151
You can adjust the fan speed too.

228
00:15:11,176 --> 00:15:13,465
Nice. And the direction.

229
00:15:13,490 --> 00:15:15,854
No more hot air
blowing from a fan.

230
00:15:15,879 --> 00:15:17,688
Excellent.

231
00:15:24,586 --> 00:15:26,073
Beautiful shot.

232
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:28,160
Very nice.

233
00:15:29,233 --> 00:15:32,907
♪ It's plain to see ♪

234
00:15:33,410 --> 00:15:35,071
♪ I know exactly
what you think of me ♪

235
00:15:35,096 --> 00:15:37,670
♪ First to watch my stories
every time ♪

236
00:15:37,695 --> 00:15:40,054
Hey, table three is ready to go!

237
00:15:40,079 --> 00:15:41,467
Don't keep the customers waiting.

238
00:15:41,492 --> 00:15:43,031
Table ten, listen up.

239
00:15:43,055 --> 00:15:46,320
The customer is allergic
to garlic. No garlic.

240
00:15:46,345 --> 00:15:48,923
And this Date on the Green set
is really important.

241
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:52,341
When they take photos,
I want a million views!

242
00:15:52,366 --> 00:15:54,470
- Yes, Chef.
- Good.

243
00:15:54,544 --> 00:15:55,910
Ready?

244
00:16:01,223 --> 00:16:02,608
Give me a heart shape, please.

245
00:16:03,035 --> 00:16:05,963
♪ Giving me signs,
so why still wait? ♪

246
00:16:05,988 --> 00:16:09,434
♪ You know I'm into you, I bet ♪

247
00:16:09,459 --> 00:16:13,782
♪ How long will you keep
playing so tough? ♪

248
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:16,072
Don't force it.
Keep your lower body steady.

249
00:16:21,277 --> 00:16:22,823
I'm swinging
with everything I've got,

250
00:16:22,848 --> 00:16:24,111
and the ball barely moves.

251
00:16:24,135 --> 00:16:25,692
Focus on a good swing first.

252
00:16:26,105 --> 00:16:27,485
Let's try again.

253
00:16:32,188 --> 00:16:34,529
Wow, that was beautiful.

254
00:16:40,737 --> 00:16:42,229
Okay. Try it.

255
00:16:44,711 --> 00:16:48,188
Good. Bring your pinky in.

256
00:16:48,850 --> 00:16:52,572
Now swing. Nice! Very good.

257
00:16:53,003 --> 00:16:56,917
Great. Now let's look at
your backswing.

258
00:16:57,270 --> 00:16:59,805
Take it back,
shift your weight to the left,

259
00:16:59,830 --> 00:17:03,034
make impact,
and finish the swing.

260
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:08,644
You actually have
a really nice finish.

261
00:17:13,962 --> 00:17:15,248
Excellent.

262
00:17:18,545 --> 00:17:20,831
This hole looks insanely real.

263
00:17:20,856 --> 00:17:23,133
Yeah, playing this makes me
want to hit the real course.

264
00:17:24,527 --> 00:17:25,765
Sign up for our club today

265
00:17:25,790 --> 00:17:27,790
and you'll get
a free golf club item in-game.

266
00:17:27,965 --> 00:17:30,354
- Then sign me up.
- Welcome aboard.

267
00:17:49,095 --> 00:17:50,693
What are you smiling about?

268
00:17:53,023 --> 00:17:56,016
I'm just happy
seeing the course like this.

269
00:17:56,502 --> 00:17:58,058
It feels alive again.

270
00:18:00,227 --> 00:18:01,284
Tired?

271
00:18:03,537 --> 00:18:06,128
Yeah. But I'm not satisfied yet.

272
00:18:06,153 --> 00:18:08,306
I think we can take this
even further.

273
00:18:08,901 --> 00:18:11,538
What else do you think
we could do?

274
00:18:11,948 --> 00:18:16,272
Maybe we need
some fresh inspiration.

275
00:18:16,297 --> 00:18:19,037
Something that takes us beyond
the usual idea of a golf course.

276
00:18:33,855 --> 00:18:35,535
We're going to a fashion show?

277
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:39,275
Oh my God!
This is literally my dream.

278
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:41,349
London! Paris! Italy!

279
00:18:41,374 --> 00:18:45,359
My chance to finally
strut down the runway!

280
00:18:45,646 --> 00:18:48,515
Not on the runway, Queen.
Next to it.

281
00:18:48,540 --> 00:18:50,237
We're watching,
not modeling.

282
00:18:50,572 --> 00:18:53,251
Don't crush my dreams. Oof!

283
00:18:53,363 --> 00:18:54,814
If you weren't
the owner's daughter,

284
00:18:54,839 --> 00:18:56,451
you'd get another one! Oof!

285
00:18:57,386 --> 00:18:59,607
It's my friend's fashion show.

286
00:18:59,632 --> 00:19:01,863
But it's not just
a regular runway show.

287
00:19:02,646 --> 00:19:05,438
Ooh, something wild?
Are they going naked?

288
00:19:05,463 --> 00:19:08,433
It's a fashion show, Queen.
There have to be clothes.

289
00:19:08,789 --> 00:19:11,230
And you! Nothing you say
is music to my ears either!

290
00:19:11,255 --> 00:19:13,780
Honestly, you should be
coming to work naked!

291
00:19:13,805 --> 00:19:15,474
That's more my style.

292
00:19:16,109 --> 00:19:18,125
You'll all find out
when we get there.

293
00:19:18,150 --> 00:19:21,700
But for this event, I want
everyone dressed to the nines.

294
00:19:23,387 --> 00:19:26,658
Can I sit this one out? I'm
not really into events like that.

295
00:19:26,683 --> 00:19:29,652
Nope. We need to get out there
and open our minds to new things,

296
00:19:29,677 --> 00:19:32,760
not just golf, golf,
and more golf.

297
00:19:32,785 --> 00:19:34,407
Exactly.

298
00:19:34,432 --> 00:19:37,734
And don't worry about your look.
I'll take care of everything.

299
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:40,196
Don't forget, I studied fashion.

300
00:19:40,731 --> 00:19:43,503
Everyone has to look fabulous.
Vas-y!

301
00:19:43,528 --> 00:19:46,685
- Huh? Vas-what?
- Just say it.

302
00:19:47,219 --> 00:19:50,302
- Vas-y!
- Vas-y!

303
00:19:52,456 --> 00:19:53,717
What the hell does that mean?

304
00:19:53,742 --> 00:19:56,036
- Beats the hell outta me.
- Huh?

305
00:20:01,114 --> 00:20:04,039
I don't think
a dress like this would suit me.

306
00:20:04,064 --> 00:20:06,430
- Says who?
- Me.

307
00:20:07,519 --> 00:20:10,347
- Do you ever look in the mirror?
- Every day.

308
00:20:10,547 --> 00:20:12,906
And you still don't know
how beautiful you are?

309
00:20:12,931 --> 00:20:14,829
Please try it on for me.

310
00:20:14,854 --> 00:20:18,379
It's an evening gown I designed
and had made a while ago,

311
00:20:18,404 --> 00:20:20,993
but I've never found a model
it fit quite right.

312
00:20:21,018 --> 00:20:24,306
Please?
Just try it on for me.

313
00:20:25,783 --> 00:20:28,248
You want me to try it on
right here?

314
00:20:28,273 --> 00:20:29,860
Yes. I'll help you zip it up.

315
00:20:29,885 --> 00:20:31,377
I think I'll change
in the bathroom.

316
00:20:45,044 --> 00:20:46,125
Are you done yet?

317
00:20:46,149 --> 00:20:48,794
I haven't even put it on yet.
What's the rush?

318
00:20:48,819 --> 00:20:51,073
I just want to see
how it looks on you.

319
00:20:51,098 --> 00:20:53,876
When I designed this,
I revised it so many times.

320
00:20:53,901 --> 00:20:56,365
I kept wondering where
I'd find the right model for it.

321
00:20:56,390 --> 00:20:58,192
But I think
it'll look perfect on you.

322
00:20:58,217 --> 00:21:00,091
Are you done? Want me to help?

323
00:21:00,116 --> 00:21:02,854
It's tricky to put on. Pro Vee!

324
00:21:04,846 --> 00:21:06,114
Pro Vee?

325
00:21:07,902 --> 00:21:09,830
Are you done yet?

326
00:21:10,683 --> 00:21:11,882
Done yet?

327
00:21:14,154 --> 00:21:15,614
I want to see.

328
00:21:16,166 --> 00:21:19,175
Want me to help? I can help you.

329
00:21:46,637 --> 00:21:47,817
So beautiful.

330
00:21:48,802 --> 00:21:51,690
The dress or me?

331
00:21:52,894 --> 00:21:55,880
A dress doesn't make
a woman beautiful.

332
00:21:55,905 --> 00:21:58,882
It fills with a beautiful
she already has.

333
00:21:58,907 --> 00:22:02,500
I still remember that line
from my first design class.

334
00:22:02,525 --> 00:22:04,324
A dress doesn't make
a woman beautiful.

335
00:22:04,349 --> 00:22:06,869
It simply reveals
the beauty she already has.

336
00:22:06,894 --> 00:22:07,943
So, is it beautiful?

337
00:22:11,096 --> 00:22:13,280
Come here.
I'll zip you up.

338
00:22:23,642 --> 00:22:25,462
You have such a beautiful back.

339
00:22:25,835 --> 00:22:28,446
You're the first person
who's ever complimented my back.

340
00:22:29,031 --> 00:22:30,911
For the show, wear your hair up

341
00:22:30,936 --> 00:22:32,681
and show off
your shoulders and back.

342
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:36,243
Why do I need
to show them off to anyone?

343
00:22:36,727 --> 00:22:39,539
We don't dress up
for other people.

344
00:22:39,564 --> 00:22:40,861
Then what for?

345
00:22:42,035 --> 00:22:45,544
To show that we're proud
of what we have.

346
00:22:45,569 --> 00:22:48,381
Why should we hide
our own beauty?

347
00:22:51,114 --> 00:22:52,291
Look in the mirror.

348
00:22:57,070 --> 00:23:00,052
The dress is beautiful.
I love it.

349
00:23:02,479 --> 00:23:05,019
I should be thanking you.

350
00:23:05,044 --> 00:23:07,067
You finally brought this dress
back to life

351
00:23:07,092 --> 00:23:09,092
after all these years.

352
00:23:10,699 --> 00:23:16,314
You've brought a lot of things
around here back to life.

353
00:23:28,802 --> 00:23:30,642
Pick one. Left or right?

354
00:23:30,952 --> 00:23:32,952
Either one. You choose for me.

355
00:23:33,073 --> 00:23:34,200
Hmm.

356
00:23:38,803 --> 00:23:40,453
This one suits your skin tone.

357
00:23:40,478 --> 00:23:42,045
- Take this, Pro Jin.
- Okay.

358
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:44,895
I'll go get a garment bag for it.

359
00:23:47,739 --> 00:23:50,490
This place is pretty big.
How many rooms are there?

360
00:23:51,903 --> 00:23:55,859
Two bedrooms, both en suite,
and a living room.

361
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:59,353
- You live here alone?
- Yes.

362
00:24:03,634 --> 00:24:05,100
Have you eaten yet?

363
00:24:05,512 --> 00:24:07,369
You mean dinner?

364
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,227
- Yeah.
- Not yet.

365
00:24:10,606 --> 00:24:11,986
Want to grab something to eat?

366
00:24:24,595 --> 00:24:27,900
Oh, Mr. Manager!
You really are here.

367
00:24:27,925 --> 00:24:31,253
Oh, Chef. What can I do for you?

368
00:24:32,086 --> 00:24:35,645
Well, I do need something.
But just the two of us here...

369
00:24:35,670 --> 00:24:38,014
What if people
get the wrong idea?

370
00:24:38,039 --> 00:24:40,676
- I don't think they will.
- I'm kidding.

371
00:24:40,846 --> 00:24:43,187
Miss Nana asked me
to bring you this outfit.

372
00:24:43,362 --> 00:24:46,923
Oh, thanks.
Where's yours, Chef Queen?

373
00:24:47,650 --> 00:24:50,087
Oh, no. No one can see mine yet.

374
00:24:50,112 --> 00:24:52,587
You'll see it at the event.
It's a surprise.

375
00:24:53,930 --> 00:24:56,166
Chef Queen,
take a look at this.

376
00:24:56,563 --> 00:24:59,999
Isn't that our former manager?

377
00:25:02,835 --> 00:25:07,722
That's March!
And that's Ms. Yupadee's course.

378
00:25:07,926 --> 00:25:10,940
So he ended up leeching off
Ms. Yupadee's course after all.

379
00:25:12,089 --> 00:25:14,841
Guys like him always find
a way to survive. Impressive.

380
00:25:19,153 --> 00:25:22,580
I've approved
the project you proposed.

381
00:25:23,479 --> 00:25:25,923
Thank you. You can count on me.

382
00:25:26,253 --> 00:25:30,723
Do you know who Good View
hired to replace you?

383
00:25:31,636 --> 00:25:35,262
His name is Nut.
He comes from the hotel business.

384
00:25:35,287 --> 00:25:36,945
He's never managed
a golf course before.

385
00:25:42,734 --> 00:25:44,637
I guess they couldn't find
anyone better.

386
00:25:45,415 --> 00:25:48,552
After all, the one person who
knows that place inside and out

387
00:25:49,890 --> 00:25:51,626
is already here
at The Royal Green.

388
00:25:55,287 --> 00:25:59,046
Keep a close eye on everything
happening at Good View.

389
00:26:00,029 --> 00:26:03,931
I want that course
for the lowest possible price.

390
00:26:05,751 --> 00:26:06,841
You got it.

391
00:26:14,908 --> 00:26:17,712
- Here you go. Rice noodles...
- This is the place you picked?

392
00:26:17,737 --> 00:26:19,545
- Yep.
- Enjoy.

393
00:26:19,570 --> 00:26:21,188
Why didn't we go somewhere nicer?

394
00:26:21,834 --> 00:26:23,329
What's wrong with this place?

395
00:26:24,360 --> 00:26:26,312
It's cheap, simple, quick,

396
00:26:26,337 --> 00:26:28,717
convenient, filling,
and delicious.

397
00:26:32,013 --> 00:26:34,195
- Two chicken noodles, please.
- Sure.

398
00:26:34,220 --> 00:26:36,255
Dry or with soup today?

399
00:26:36,805 --> 00:26:38,567
Pro Jin, dry or with soup?

400
00:26:38,592 --> 00:26:40,234
Whatever you're having.

401
00:26:40,829 --> 00:26:42,969
And some soup on the side.

402
00:26:42,994 --> 00:26:44,994
Sure. Have a seat.

403
00:26:48,086 --> 00:26:50,469
You have a way of making
everything seem so simple.

404
00:26:51,288 --> 00:26:54,647
I just choose whatever
makes life less complicated.

405
00:26:54,854 --> 00:26:56,544
Do you normally eat
at places like this?

406
00:26:56,729 --> 00:26:58,717
Sure. Why?

407
00:26:58,742 --> 00:27:01,465
You seem more like
the expensive-dining type.

408
00:27:01,893 --> 00:27:03,605
I can do expensive too.

409
00:27:03,630 --> 00:27:05,985
But expensive
doesn't always mean delicious.

410
00:27:06,390 --> 00:27:10,012
Sometimes simple food like this
is much more comforting.

411
00:27:11,666 --> 00:27:14,692
You don't look like a golf course
CEO's right-hand woman now.

412
00:27:15,975 --> 00:27:18,134
Why? What do I look like?

413
00:27:19,073 --> 00:27:22,708
Like a third-year student
who just finished an assignment

414
00:27:22,733 --> 00:27:24,538
and came out for noodles
by her dorm.

415
00:27:25,831 --> 00:27:28,110
You don't look much
like a golf pro either.

416
00:27:29,252 --> 00:27:32,464
- What do I look like, then?
- Hmm...

417
00:27:32,807 --> 00:27:37,084
Like a senior
trying to hit on a junior,

418
00:27:37,109 --> 00:27:39,840
but he's broke, so he takes her

419
00:27:39,865 --> 00:27:41,865
for street-side noodles
instead of fine dining.

420
00:27:43,318 --> 00:27:49,274
And after dinner, where does
this senior take his junior next?

421
00:27:51,779 --> 00:27:53,345
Now we're getting
a little R-rated.

422
00:27:58,868 --> 00:28:03,282
Here we go! Two dry noodles.

423
00:28:03,307 --> 00:28:06,375
- And your usual soup.
- Thank you.

424
00:28:07,290 --> 00:28:09,475
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

425
00:28:09,500 --> 00:28:12,080
Want me to pick up
some dumplings for you?

426
00:28:12,105 --> 00:28:14,533
No, thanks.
I can do the picking up myself.

427
00:28:17,334 --> 00:28:21,222
Ooh, you've got game!
All right, flirt away!

428
00:28:40,651 --> 00:28:41,696
Good?

429
00:29:00,755 --> 00:29:02,737
- Hey, Nana.
- Are you dressed yet?

430
00:29:02,762 --> 00:29:05,642
- Dressed for what?
- The fashion show I mentioned.

431
00:29:05,667 --> 00:29:08,695
That's today? Do I have to go?

432
00:29:08,720 --> 00:29:11,832
Five o'clock.
We leave on the dot.

433
00:29:12,583 --> 00:29:13,651
Yeah, yeah.

434
00:29:30,967 --> 00:29:34,085
Thank you.
All set. Thank you.

435
00:30:12,604 --> 00:30:16,233
- Congratulations!
- Thank you. See you inside.

436
00:30:16,258 --> 00:30:19,242
Thank you. Oh, Nana!

437
00:30:20,535 --> 00:30:27,163
Hello, Fahsai!
Fashion's hottest rising star.

438
00:30:27,479 --> 00:30:29,773
Thank you for making time for us,

439
00:30:29,797 --> 00:30:33,606
Miss Nana
of Good View Golf Course.

440
00:30:33,631 --> 00:30:37,193
Of course I'm here. Don't forget,
fashion is my world.

441
00:30:37,218 --> 00:30:42,727
I've just stepped off the runway
to run a fairway for a while.

442
00:30:44,275 --> 00:30:47,250
This is my team. I brought them
here for some inspiration.

443
00:30:47,275 --> 00:30:49,457
Maybe we'll find some ideas
we can use at the course.

444
00:30:49,482 --> 00:30:51,227
Welcome, everyone.

445
00:30:51,252 --> 00:30:54,281
It's been ages. You're
as beautiful as ever, Fahsai.

446
00:30:54,546 --> 00:30:55,768
Thank you, Nut.

447
00:30:55,792 --> 00:30:58,967
I heard you're helping Nana
run the course now.

448
00:30:59,174 --> 00:31:01,138
He's practically
the backbone of the place.

449
00:31:01,582 --> 00:31:04,720
This is Chef Queen,
our head chef.

450
00:31:04,994 --> 00:31:06,620
- Hello.
- Hello.

451
00:31:06,645 --> 00:31:08,527
You look gorgeous tonight.

452
00:31:08,551 --> 00:31:11,051
- Just a little something.
- Queen!

453
00:31:11,747 --> 00:31:14,374
- This is Belle, my assistant.
- Hello.

454
00:31:14,399 --> 00:31:18,265
This is Pro Jin, Pro Vee,
and this is Gus.

455
00:31:18,290 --> 00:31:21,015
And our handsome caddies.

456
00:31:21,999 --> 00:31:23,626
Make yourselves at home.

457
00:31:24,408 --> 00:31:27,840
Hey, all the pros
at your course are gorgeous.

458
00:31:28,070 --> 00:31:30,725
What a shame.
If I'd met them sooner,

459
00:31:30,750 --> 00:31:33,223
I'd have put them
in tonight's show.

460
00:31:38,172 --> 00:31:42,312
But this course
does have one hot chef.

461
00:31:42,337 --> 00:31:45,404
Think I could model?
I've got the look, right?

462
00:31:45,796 --> 00:31:47,988
One size fits all, girl.
That's the way to go.

463
00:31:48,013 --> 00:31:49,742
Werk! Werk!

464
00:31:49,766 --> 00:31:54,613
Feel free to do it
at my course sometime.

465
00:31:54,638 --> 00:31:57,386
- You mean... do the catering?
- ใช่

466
00:31:57,411 --> 00:32:01,586
Let's stick to catering.
Do me and...Bam! Lights out!

467
00:32:02,945 --> 00:32:06,518
Okay, everyone, enjoy yourselves.
Let's head inside.

468
00:32:07,109 --> 00:32:09,959
- We can talk inside. This way.
- You look gorgeous.

469
00:32:09,984 --> 00:32:13,326
- Girl, the new collection!
- You look amazing tonight.

470
00:33:58,750 --> 00:34:01,735
- Beautiful.
- Gorgeous.

471
00:34:27,764 --> 00:34:29,227
It's beautiful, isn't it,
Pro Vee?

472
00:34:29,973 --> 00:34:32,403
Yeah. It's interesting.

473
00:34:32,428 --> 00:34:36,874
Normally, cars and fashion
are presented separately.

474
00:34:36,899 --> 00:34:39,052
Each has its own story.

475
00:34:39,189 --> 00:34:42,618
People may lose interest
because it's nothing new.

476
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:45,670
But put them together,
and you create something new.

477
00:34:46,877 --> 00:34:51,232
What's even more interesting
is how it attracts new audiences.

478
00:34:51,653 --> 00:34:55,503
Both car enthusiasts
and people interested in fashion.

479
00:34:57,814 --> 00:34:59,295
What are you thinking, Nana?

480
00:35:00,002 --> 00:35:03,155
If a vintage garage
can become a runway,

481
00:35:03,180 --> 00:35:04,776
what about our fairway?

482
00:35:07,700 --> 00:35:08,900
What could it become?

483
00:35:12,210 --> 00:35:14,842
I'm gonna go to
the restroom real quick.

484
00:35:33,746 --> 00:35:35,955
Oh, Fahsai.

485
00:35:38,116 --> 00:35:42,961
Pro Vee, perfect timing.
I could use a little help.

486
00:35:42,986 --> 00:35:43,998
Yes?

487
00:35:44,022 --> 00:35:48,103
My zipper's stuck.
I can't get it to budge.

488
00:35:48,128 --> 00:35:50,128
Could you help me?

489
00:35:50,955 --> 00:35:52,011
Sure.

490
00:36:04,301 --> 00:36:10,044
Thank you. I'd better get back
to my guests. See you inside.

491
00:36:10,674 --> 00:36:12,462
- Sure.
- Thank you.

492
00:36:27,408 --> 00:36:30,584
Fahsai, tonight's show
was amazing.

493
00:36:30,609 --> 00:36:33,945
I loved how you paired
the fashion with the cars.

494
00:36:33,970 --> 00:36:36,846
Thanks. I'm glad you liked it.

495
00:36:36,871 --> 00:36:38,735
I've always trusted your taste.

496
00:36:38,877 --> 00:36:42,428
- You just gave me an idea.
- An idea? What kind?

497
00:36:43,241 --> 00:36:45,418
I'm putting on a fashion show
at the golf course.

498
00:36:46,688 --> 00:36:48,735
I'm turning the fairway
into a runway.

499
00:36:48,760 --> 00:36:51,180
Ooh, interesting. I like it.

500
00:36:51,205 --> 00:36:53,736
That'll be the longest runway
I've ever seen.

501
00:36:53,785 --> 00:36:56,996
It'll take the models all day
just to walk the whole thing.

502
00:36:57,337 --> 00:36:59,585
I'm not kidding. I'm serious.

503
00:36:59,610 --> 00:37:02,413
- Be my consultant.
- Sure. No problem.

504
00:37:08,975 --> 00:37:10,873
Did you enjoy the show, Pro Vee?

505
00:37:11,547 --> 00:37:14,224
- It was beautiful.
- Thank you.

506
00:37:19,682 --> 00:37:22,885
We should probably get going now.

507
00:37:22,910 --> 00:37:27,215
Don't forget about the golf
course runway. I'm serious.

508
00:37:28,646 --> 00:37:31,298
I won't. I'll come by the course.

509
00:37:32,684 --> 00:37:35,653
You'd better! I'm waiting
to show off my skills.

510
00:37:35,916 --> 00:37:39,249
- I will.
- I'll be ready to welcome you.

511
00:37:39,658 --> 00:37:42,991
All right. See you soon.

512
00:37:58,372 --> 00:38:00,926
You've insisted on
driving me home twice now.

513
00:38:01,187 --> 00:38:04,768
Should I take that
as a sign, Pro Jin?

514
00:38:07,370 --> 00:38:10,427
I'll pay you for both rides
today and last time.

515
00:38:10,657 --> 00:38:13,421
- It's fine.
- How is it fine?

516
00:38:13,769 --> 00:38:15,568
You said
you'd charge me interest too.

517
00:38:16,380 --> 00:38:18,643
Consider it payment
for finding me an outfit today.

518
00:38:18,917 --> 00:38:22,006
Miss Nana found the outfit,
not me.

519
00:38:22,363 --> 00:38:24,173
Let me transfer you the fare.

520
00:38:24,198 --> 00:38:26,670
I feel bad making you
drive me home twice.

521
00:38:26,695 --> 00:38:29,957
Don't overthink it.
We're coworkers.

522
00:38:29,982 --> 00:38:32,254
Coworkers. Not friends.

523
00:38:34,502 --> 00:38:35,763
Want to be friends?

524
00:38:36,875 --> 00:38:38,146
So you're not flirting with me.

525
00:38:52,837 --> 00:38:53,925
Wait.

526
00:38:58,999 --> 00:39:00,004
What was that?

527
00:39:02,181 --> 00:39:03,292
Nothing.

528
00:39:03,662 --> 00:39:06,575
Why do you suddenly
want to be friends with me?

529
00:39:07,979 --> 00:39:09,476
Why can't we be?

530
00:39:10,397 --> 00:39:12,405
Is there a limit
on how many friends you can have?

531
00:39:13,486 --> 00:39:14,836
Well... no.

532
00:39:15,896 --> 00:39:17,388
Then that's a yes.

533
00:39:19,126 --> 00:39:20,205
Fine.

534
00:39:21,271 --> 00:39:24,839
Then thanks
for driving me home twice.

535
00:39:26,183 --> 00:39:27,992
I'll drive you home
as many times as you want.

536
00:39:31,866 --> 00:39:33,358
When do I have to
return this dress?

537
00:39:33,383 --> 00:39:34,421
As soon as possible.

538
00:39:34,446 --> 00:39:35,785
Want me to take it off
right here?

539
00:39:35,810 --> 00:39:38,557
Hey! No. Tomorrow's fine.

540
00:39:45,134 --> 00:39:46,202
Good night.

541
00:40:14,030 --> 00:40:17,584
Abigail, get those ready.
Oh, that's wrapped beautifully.

542
00:40:17,609 --> 00:40:20,865
Just not quite fast enough.
Come on, customers are coming!

543
00:40:22,566 --> 00:40:23,679
Nana!

544
00:40:23,704 --> 00:40:25,695
- Fahsai!
- Hi.

545
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,213
You didn't tell me
you were coming.

546
00:40:27,238 --> 00:40:29,737
I had some business nearby,
so I thought I'd stop by.

547
00:40:29,762 --> 00:40:32,917
And we can talk about
that fashion show idea of yours.

548
00:40:32,942 --> 00:40:36,277
Oh, you're putting on a fashion
show at the golf course?

549
00:40:36,302 --> 00:40:38,822
It's just an idea for now, Queen.

550
00:40:38,847 --> 00:40:41,045
Is Pro Vee here today?

551
00:40:42,308 --> 00:40:44,198
Oh! Perfect timing.

552
00:40:44,490 --> 00:40:47,568
Hi, Fahsai. Here for a round?

553
00:40:47,624 --> 00:40:49,145
I'm here to look around.

554
00:40:49,170 --> 00:40:52,008
Nana wants to put on
a fashion show here.

555
00:40:52,972 --> 00:40:56,814
Looks like I'll need you
to show me around today.

556
00:40:59,059 --> 00:41:01,129
Pro Vee probably has lessons.

557
00:41:03,155 --> 00:41:06,428
I'm free right now. My next
lesson isn't until this evening.

558
00:41:07,927 --> 00:41:09,133
Perfect.

559
00:41:09,158 --> 00:41:12,900
Perfect for you too, Miss Nana.
You're free right now.

560
00:41:12,925 --> 00:41:14,877
Go with your best friend.

561
00:41:14,902 --> 00:41:18,791
You still have urgent documents
to review, Miss Nana.

562
00:41:18,816 --> 00:41:20,283
They're not finished yet.

563
00:41:26,339 --> 00:41:28,434
Nana, you don't have to come.

564
00:41:28,458 --> 00:41:31,455
Pro Vee and I
can go by ourselves.

565
00:41:33,249 --> 00:41:35,114
- Shall we?
- Sure.

566
00:41:35,519 --> 00:41:36,542
Okay.

567
00:41:46,475 --> 00:41:50,674
Looks like your best friend
is about to steal your girl.

568
00:41:57,531 --> 00:42:00,701
This golf course
is actually really beautiful.

569
00:42:01,507 --> 00:42:05,224
The green grass
against the blue sky,

570
00:42:05,249 --> 00:42:08,074
the hills, the water...

571
00:42:10,098 --> 00:42:12,342
Do you play golf, Fahsai?

572
00:42:12,770 --> 00:42:16,138
I don't really exercise at all.
It's exhausting.

573
00:42:16,163 --> 00:42:19,547
It's hot, you get all sticky...
not my idea of fun.

574
00:42:20,079 --> 00:42:23,766
Give golf a try.
I promise you'll fall for it.

575
00:42:24,067 --> 00:42:25,331
Now that sounds interesting.

576
00:42:25,996 --> 00:42:28,420
I wouldn't mind falling.

577
00:42:29,967 --> 00:42:33,886
Then once you get the hang of it,
you should come play a round.

578
00:42:34,130 --> 00:42:38,287
If you're just starting out,
you could begin with nine holes

579
00:42:38,312 --> 00:42:41,220
and finish over there. See?

580
00:42:41,561 --> 00:42:43,875
What are those two
whispering about over there?

581
00:42:45,487 --> 00:42:47,010
What are you staring at,
Miss Nana?

582
00:42:48,727 --> 00:42:49,759
Nothing.

583
00:42:49,999 --> 00:42:53,818
Maybe you should take a look
at your own heart instead.

584
00:42:53,843 --> 00:42:57,406
It's running hotter
than this fairway right now.

585
00:43:00,155 --> 00:43:01,200
Queen!

586
00:43:02,731 --> 00:43:05,973
Are you jealous over your friend
or over your pro?

587
00:43:06,309 --> 00:43:09,395
Don't answer. I already know.

588
00:43:12,046 --> 00:43:16,268
Would an area like that
be available for us to use?

589
00:43:16,375 --> 00:43:17,667
It does look beautiful.

590
00:43:17,692 --> 00:43:21,441
We may need to ask
your friend who owns the course.

591
00:43:21,590 --> 00:43:25,524
- Ooh, are they about to hug?
- Queen!

592
00:43:26,090 --> 00:43:29,393
Maybe even kiss... Ow!

593
00:43:46,334 --> 00:43:47,971
Where's Eve?
We had a lesson scheduled.

594
00:43:47,996 --> 00:43:51,170
She said she doesn't like
waiting, so she already left.

595
00:43:51,195 --> 00:43:54,125
Why were you late today?
She was a new client too.

596
00:43:54,150 --> 00:43:57,017
They closed a road,
so traffic was backed up.

597
00:44:03,646 --> 00:44:06,180
Oh, Pro Jin. What's up?

598
00:44:06,363 --> 00:44:08,928
I wanted to apologize.

599
00:44:09,358 --> 00:44:10,907
For being late today?

600
00:44:11,082 --> 00:44:13,796
Yes. We ended up
losing a client because of me.

601
00:44:13,982 --> 00:44:15,831
I already called her.

602
00:44:15,855 --> 00:44:17,914
I threw in an extra hour,
and she calmed down.

603
00:44:18,818 --> 00:44:20,271
Just don't be late again.

604
00:44:22,947 --> 00:44:26,326
I wanted to ask
about the staff housing.

605
00:44:26,926 --> 00:44:30,578
Would it be possible
for me to stay here too?

606
00:44:30,603 --> 00:44:32,453
My place is pretty far away,

607
00:44:32,682 --> 00:44:35,790
and if housing is provided
for the golf pros here,

608
00:44:35,815 --> 00:44:38,377
I figured
I might be eligible too.

609
00:44:39,299 --> 00:44:43,219
Well, it's not exactly
an official benefit.

610
00:44:43,664 --> 00:44:45,902
We just try to help
where we can.

611
00:44:46,734 --> 00:44:50,241
But I think all the houses
are occupied now. Right, Belle?

612
00:44:50,681 --> 00:44:53,584
Mm. Yes.

613
00:44:54,841 --> 00:44:56,547
The houses are full,

614
00:44:56,571 --> 00:44:59,368
but I think
there's still a spare bedroom.

615
00:45:01,203 --> 00:45:02,299
What do you mean?

616
00:45:03,217 --> 00:45:05,906
There's a two-bedroom house

617
00:45:05,931 --> 00:45:08,272
with only one person
living in it.

618
00:45:41,785 --> 00:45:45,361
So, Aom, give us an update.
How's married life?

619
00:45:45,829 --> 00:45:47,775
Still fabulous.

620
00:45:47,800 --> 00:45:49,378
You girls should try
marriage sometime.

621
00:45:49,403 --> 00:45:51,558
- Let's hope it stays fabulous.

622
00:45:52,103 --> 00:45:55,095
Fahsai, look at that
dreamy little smile.

623
00:45:55,120 --> 00:45:56,465
There's definitely someone.

624
00:45:56,489 --> 00:46:01,426
Exactly. Normally, our Fahsai
never shuts up.

625
00:46:01,451 --> 00:46:06,107
Come on, tell us.
Who's the poor guy?

626
00:46:06,976 --> 00:46:13,156
We met at my runway show,
and again just now.

627
00:46:13,181 --> 00:46:15,340
What? Who?

628
00:46:15,365 --> 00:46:17,469
Then we must've met too.

629
00:46:17,494 --> 00:46:19,494
Exactly. Who is it, Fahsai?

630
00:46:21,355 --> 00:46:23,870
A pro golfer.

631
00:46:26,729 --> 00:46:32,278
Ooh, so you're leaving the runway
for the fairway now, bestie?

632
00:46:32,839 --> 00:46:35,414
Oh, stop it.
Just eat. What did you order?

633
00:46:35,439 --> 00:46:37,232
- Come on, tell us everything.
- No.

634
00:46:37,257 --> 00:46:39,935
- So? How's the swing?
- Spill!

635
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:42,735
I said we met at a fashion show.
What swing?

636
00:46:42,760 --> 00:46:44,339
Are you sure? Be honest.

637
00:46:44,363 --> 00:46:46,129
Just eat. Why are you
so obsessed with me?

638
00:46:46,154 --> 00:46:49,396
- Have some cake first.
- Tell us! We want to know.

639
00:46:49,421 --> 00:46:52,934
- Come on, tell us!
- Right now!

640
00:46:59,395 --> 00:47:01,466
Am I making you uncomfortable

641
00:47:01,491 --> 00:47:04,006
or invading your privacy
by moving in?

642
00:47:04,438 --> 00:47:07,806
- Don't overthink it.
- Then, thank you.

643
00:47:09,238 --> 00:47:11,109
But I do have
some house rules.

644
00:47:11,593 --> 00:47:12,799
Let's hear them.

645
00:47:12,824 --> 00:47:15,021
One, no practicing golf indoors.

646
00:47:15,172 --> 00:47:17,955
Two, don't leave
the lights on all night.

647
00:47:18,026 --> 00:47:20,245
Three, no overnight guests.

648
00:47:20,270 --> 00:47:23,637
- Are these course rules or...
- My rules.

649
00:47:25,258 --> 00:47:27,659
Deal. You were here first.

650
00:47:28,222 --> 00:47:29,486
Thank you.

651
00:47:29,511 --> 00:47:31,599
- But the same goes for you.
- What does?

652
00:47:31,624 --> 00:47:33,172
No overnight guests.

653
00:47:33,436 --> 00:47:35,007
I don't have anyone anyway.

654
00:47:35,698 --> 00:47:37,380
- You're single?
- Mm-hmm.

655
00:47:38,190 --> 00:47:40,232
So am I.

656
00:47:53,531 --> 00:47:59,561
Food's here, Miss Nana!
And it looks amazing.

657
00:48:00,732 --> 00:48:04,170
Aren't you busy, Chef?
Why are you serving it yourself?

658
00:48:04,273 --> 00:48:07,107
Oh, the kitchen
is absolutely slammed today.

659
00:48:07,132 --> 00:48:08,806
We can barely keep up.

660
00:48:09,507 --> 00:48:12,179
Let the others take a break.
I can handle this.

661
00:48:12,888 --> 00:48:15,133
But Miss Nana,
what are you doing up here?

662
00:48:15,158 --> 00:48:18,701
So much work you can't
even eat at the clubhouse?

663
00:48:18,726 --> 00:48:21,990
I'm working on some plans.
I got a little carried away.

664
00:48:22,746 --> 00:48:26,151
Don't spend
all your time working.

665
00:48:26,429 --> 00:48:28,718
You might regret it later.

666
00:48:29,021 --> 00:48:30,411
What do you mean?

667
00:48:30,618 --> 00:48:33,597
Someone you know very well

668
00:48:33,622 --> 00:48:36,240
just signed up for golf lessons.

669
00:48:37,412 --> 00:48:41,118
And right now, they're enjoying
each other...oops,

670
00:48:42,303 --> 00:48:45,282
I mean, enjoying a meal
at the clubhouse.

671
00:48:45,713 --> 00:48:46,864
Who?

672
00:48:49,420 --> 00:48:51,807
Clear Sky.

673
00:48:53,069 --> 00:48:54,889
Clear... Sky?

674
00:48:54,914 --> 00:48:57,684
Clear. Sky.

675
00:48:59,859 --> 00:49:01,128
Fahsai!

676
00:49:03,411 --> 00:49:04,805
Eating alone?

677
00:49:12,848 --> 00:49:17,118
Careful, don't knock that over.
I made it especially for you.

678
00:49:17,143 --> 00:49:18,298
I won't.

679
00:49:34,173 --> 00:49:35,958
I'm not sure either.

680
00:49:36,301 --> 00:49:39,420
- Would you like some shrimp?
- Thank you.

681
00:49:47,250 --> 00:49:50,361
- Feeling possessive?
- Jealous.

682
00:49:55,234 --> 00:49:57,361
Queen, you put laxatives
in that, right?

683
00:49:57,687 --> 00:49:59,571
Oh! I could never do that!

684
00:49:59,596 --> 00:50:01,994
That violates
the global chef code of ethics!

685
00:50:04,015 --> 00:50:06,675
But how about this?

686
00:50:06,700 --> 00:50:09,484
I'll have someone carry over
a bright-colored drink,

687
00:50:09,509 --> 00:50:13,209
Then... Oops!
Spill it all over them.

688
00:50:13,234 --> 00:50:15,051
That way,
they'll have to split up.

689
00:50:15,076 --> 00:50:17,076
Good idea, right?

690
00:50:18,816 --> 00:50:21,773
I'm not the villain here, Queen.

691
00:50:25,647 --> 00:50:27,263
I'm the heroine.

692
00:50:30,202 --> 00:50:33,705
"Pro Vee, try this.
It's really good."

693
00:50:33,730 --> 00:50:36,985
"Sure. It must be delicious."

694
00:50:37,197 --> 00:50:39,260
Give it a minute.
They'll be all over each other.

695
00:50:43,643 --> 00:50:49,291
Calm down. Calm down, girl.
Calm down.

696
00:50:50,751 --> 00:50:52,132
Hold it like this.

697
00:50:53,060 --> 00:50:55,664
That's right.
and put your right hand over it.

698
00:50:56,707 --> 00:50:59,532
Even holding the club
properly is hard.

699
00:51:02,332 --> 00:51:05,523
Pro Vee, you hold golf clubs
every day.

700
00:51:05,548 --> 00:51:08,137
How are your hands still so soft?

701
00:51:23,357 --> 00:51:26,342
Carry over a bright-colored
drink, serve it to them,

702
00:51:26,367 --> 00:51:28,794
and spill the whole thing.

703
00:51:28,819 --> 00:51:30,654
That way,
they'll have to split up.

704
00:51:30,813 --> 00:51:33,059
I'm not the villain here, Queen.

705
00:51:34,050 --> 00:51:35,638
I'm the heroine.

706
00:51:35,663 --> 00:51:38,893
She went in with a vengeance,

707
00:51:38,918 --> 00:51:42,198
determined to complete
her mission.

708
00:51:48,416 --> 00:51:52,127
Whoosh! Villain-in-training.

709
00:51:54,304 --> 00:51:56,460
Nana, what are you doing
over there?

710
00:51:56,936 --> 00:51:58,256
Are you okay?

711
00:51:59,182 --> 00:52:01,871
- I'm fine. I'm fine.
- You're soaked.

712
00:52:02,805 --> 00:52:07,215
I was going to bring you
some water, but I spilled it all.

713
00:52:11,999 --> 00:52:13,098
Did you hurt yourself?

714
00:52:14,559 --> 00:52:17,376
I'm fine. It's nothing.

715
00:52:19,871 --> 00:52:23,294
Guess your revenge
wasn't strong enough, Miss Nana.

716
00:52:38,329 --> 00:52:42,092
Are you tired? You've been
awfully quiet since Fahsai left.

717
00:52:42,623 --> 00:52:43,642
No.

718
00:52:44,963 --> 00:52:48,154
Pro Vee, can I ask you something
straight?

719
00:52:48,709 --> 00:52:49,719
Sure.

720
00:52:51,841 --> 00:52:53,630
What do you think of Fahsai?

721
00:52:53,836 --> 00:52:56,036
What do you mean?

722
00:52:56,489 --> 00:53:01,288
You've only met her a few times,

723
00:53:01,313 --> 00:53:03,137
but you two already
seem pretty close.

724
00:53:03,483 --> 00:53:04,569
Jealous?

725
00:53:11,777 --> 00:53:13,331
Yes, Fahsai?

726
00:53:15,796 --> 00:53:18,432
My schedule's packed right now.

727
00:53:18,457 --> 00:53:21,583
I'll have the course book you in
for another day.

728
00:53:21,925 --> 00:53:24,535
Sorry about that. Okay.

729
00:53:26,590 --> 00:53:28,084
You have her number too?

730
00:53:28,843 --> 00:53:30,803
I don't even have yours.

731
00:53:31,120 --> 00:53:32,377
Give me your phone.

732
00:53:48,324 --> 00:53:51,492
So... do you have feelings
for Fahsai?

733
00:53:51,904 --> 00:53:53,278
What kind of feelings?

734
00:53:55,150 --> 00:53:57,053
Do you like her?

735
00:54:00,527 --> 00:54:04,894
Why do you ask?
Are you jealous or possessive?

736
00:54:04,919 --> 00:54:06,426
Am I allowed to be?

737
00:54:07,948 --> 00:54:09,107
Allowed to be what?

738
00:54:11,068 --> 00:54:13,952
Am I allowed
to be jealous over you?

739
00:54:15,515 --> 00:54:19,011
Good question.
Do you want to be?

740
00:54:22,126 --> 00:54:25,805
If you do, you'd better
start staking your claim.

741
00:54:27,027 --> 00:54:31,328
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

742
00:54:32,143 --> 00:54:36,063
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

743
00:54:36,088 --> 00:54:38,088
(Nana's Vee)

744
00:54:38,113 --> 00:54:41,840
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

745
00:54:43,640 --> 00:54:46,190
Hello, my Nana.

746
00:54:47,437 --> 00:54:52,630
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

747
00:54:52,655 --> 00:54:56,975
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

748
00:54:57,485 --> 00:55:00,798
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

749
00:55:00,823 --> 00:55:03,349
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

750
00:55:03,374 --> 00:55:06,878
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

751
00:55:06,903 --> 00:55:11,663
I wonder if there's room here
for your Nana too.

752
00:55:11,982 --> 00:55:13,982
Have you seen the news
about Goodview's event?

753
00:55:14,776 --> 00:55:18,162
The fashion show thing?

754
00:55:18,435 --> 00:55:21,364
It's a golf course.
It's right there in the name.

755
00:55:21,389 --> 00:55:23,453
Nana must've completely lost it.

756
00:55:23,478 --> 00:55:28,210
What if that six-year-old girl
still stands by her promise

757
00:55:29,173 --> 00:55:34,383
and has come back to claim it?
What would you say, Pro Vee?

758
00:55:38,476 --> 00:55:42,691
♪ Do you know which way to go? ♪

759
00:55:43,448 --> 00:55:48,555
♪ To get us closer to our goal ♪

760
00:55:48,580 --> 00:55:53,209
♪ Together, we'll race
toward the line ♪

761
00:55:53,776 --> 00:55:58,270
♪ Chasing the dream
that's yours and mine ♪

762
00:55:58,815 --> 00:56:03,953
♪ In the end,
I know we'll make it there ♪

763
00:56:03,978 --> 00:56:08,260
♪ Just one rule
for you and me to share ♪

764
00:56:09,070 --> 00:56:12,215
♪ Promise you'll stay
close to me ♪

765
00:56:12,240 --> 00:56:14,695
♪ Hold me in your arms
so tenderly ♪

766
00:56:14,720 --> 00:56:20,254
♪ I've never bowed
to anyone in sight ♪

767
00:56:20,279 --> 00:56:23,346
♪ But for you,
I'd surrender without a fight ♪

768
00:56:23,371 --> 00:56:27,611
♪ Just take my hand
and hold it tight ♪

769
00:56:29,488 --> 00:56:32,635
♪ And walk with me
along the way ♪

770
00:56:32,660 --> 00:56:35,209
♪ No matter what it takes
to win someday ♪

771
00:56:35,234 --> 00:56:40,528
♪ Sometimes this tender heart
may despair ♪

772
00:56:41,002 --> 00:56:44,195
♪ But tell me,
why should we care? ♪

773
00:56:44,220 --> 00:56:46,548
♪ When all we need
is love that's fair ♪

774
00:56:46,573 --> 00:56:50,217
♪ In a love we share,
no one has to win or lose ♪

775
00:56:52,452 --> 00:56:56,985
♪ Let my heart answer anew ♪

776
00:56:57,602 --> 00:57:02,124
♪ A thousand rounds,
it'd still choose you ♪

777
00:57:02,689 --> 00:57:07,247
♪ One look in your eyes
is all I need ♪

778
00:57:07,560 --> 00:57:11,267
♪ Oh, baby. I trust your sweet. ♪
